                        "entry_id": "de4547bb-5f0c-37bd-b6f9-0da09c2d8862",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The top portion of a cumulonimbus cloud, which tends to be flattened or fibery in appearance, and may be indicative of thunderstorm activity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "41dfbf50-838e-46aa-bb28-813727dfd72a",
                                "sense_id": "34ac041c-b2d5-3279-84a4-5b53b5e375ce",
                                "text": "Half the sky was checkered with black thunderheads, but all the west was luminous and clear:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea4a08b3-916b-40af-8098-653496a56273",
                                "sense_id": "34ac041c-b2d5-3279-84a4-5b53b5e375ce",
                                "text": "The wisps of smoke above Léogane became dark and thick, and flowered into a towering thunderhead—an ominous cloud that drifted slowly to the westward and was constantly replenished at its base by uprushes of blacker smoke."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "282dd24c-d205-49c0-9945-c1f391032321",
                                "sense_id": "34ac041c-b2d5-3279-84a4-5b53b5e375ce",
                                "text": "The sky ahead was huge with storm: all the whiteness had gone from the thunderheads, and they rolled and swirled with sulphur yellow, sea green, smoke gray, oil black, a queasy churning miles high and as wide as the horizon."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
